/T (SAM/LSA DUMP The Security Account Manager \(SAM\) database holds the NTLM hashes of local accounts only. These can be extracted with the lsadump::sam Mimikatz module. If a common local administrator account is being used with the same password across an entire environment, this can make it very trivial to move laterally.)
/E (SAM/LSA DUMP The Security Account Manager \(SAM\) database holds the NTLM hashes of local accounts only. These can be extracted with the lsadump::sam Mimikatz module. If a common local administrator account is being used with the same password across an entire environment, this can make it very trivial to move laterally.)
